/* MakeHeap_r: intermediate level of MakeHeap, written by hand (PipelineB, refinement step), the
   component BART refines.
   Purpose: restate the result of make_heap in the form the loops establish, so that two arguments
   are made once, here, away from the loops:
   - the heap is stated from the parent, cell 2 * xx + 1 and cell 2 * xx + 2 at most cell xx, with no
     division: the kernel knows little of a / b, and the loops only need linear facts. That this form
     implies the one of MakeHeap, on (ii - 1) / 2, is proved on the positions 1..max_IDX;
   - the permutation is written cell by cell, rr(xx) = array(bij(xx)), and the composition
     (bij ; array) and the range ran(array) of MakeHeap follow from it.
   array stays the concrete variable of MakeHeap; set_cell and the initialisation are unchanged.
   As in InsertionSort_r: an INVARIANT clause restating the type of array, and an ANY, taken by a
   structure rule. The quantifiers of make_heap all use the name xx: the rule has one joker for it. */
REFINEMENT
    MakeHeap_r

REFINES
    MakeHeap

SEES
    Ctx_MakeHeap

INVARIANT
    array : (0..max_IDX) --> INT

INITIALISATION
    array := (0..max_IDX) * {0}

OPERATIONS

    set_cell(pos, value) =
    PRE
        pos : IDX &
        value : INT
    THEN
        array(pos) := value
    END;

    make_heap =
    ANY rr WHERE
        rr : (0..max_IDX) --> INT &
        !xx.(xx : 0..max_IDX & 2 * xx + 1 <= max_IDX => rr(2 * xx + 1) <= rr(xx)) &
        !xx.(xx : 0..max_IDX & 2 * xx + 2 <= max_IDX => rr(2 * xx + 2) <= rr(xx)) &
        #bij.(bij : (0..max_IDX) >->> (0..max_IDX) &
              !xx.(xx : 0..max_IDX => rr(xx) = array(bij(xx))))
    THEN
        array := rr
    END

END
